(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Background: Family members of patients with terminal illness often experience anxiety,) Tj
T*
(depression, and existential distress during caregiving transitions. Creative interventions) Tj
T*
(offer potential psychological benefits. Objective: To evaluate mandala-based artistic) Tj
T*
(engagement for enhancing psychological well-being in palliative care family members.) Tj
T*
(Methods: A total of 84 family caregivers \(mean age 52 years; 71% female\) were randomized) Tj
T*
(to either weekly mandala drawing/coloring sessions for 4 weeks \(n=42\) or standard care) Tj
T*
(control \(n=42\). Sessions occurred in quiet settings with art materials provided. The) Tj
T*
(Psychological Well-Being Scale was administered at baseline and week 4; secondary measures) Tj
T*
(included the Spiritual Well-Being Scale and quality-of-life visual analog scales. Results:) Tj
T*
